  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Motor Oil Hellas Corinth Refineries S A obligated $723M in FY2026 to date on 28 awards, with an average award size of $25.8M and year-over-year change up 31.1%. Motor Oil Hellas Corinth Refineries S A shows a multi-year pattern of federal obligations that rose from $181M in FY21 to $560M in FY22, then moved through $272M in FY23, $530M in FY24, and $551M in FY25 before reaching $723M in FY26. Petroleum Refineries is the dominant market, accounting for $723M of obligations in FY2026 to date. Other Warehousing and Storage appears as a secondary market at $148K. The current-year totals are partial, covering the fiscal year to date, and the note clarifies that the listed figures are contract obligations except where award-value totals are called out separately. This snapshot highlights the concentration of federal buying in a single NAICS and the scale of awards supporting Motor Oil Hellas Corinth Refineries S A’s FY2026 to date obligations.",
